# Claude Code — machine-local settings and state only (owner decision 5, Issue #18, 2026-07-30).
# `.claude/hooks/` is deliberately NOT here: ignoring it while tracked settings.json registered those
# hooks by path is finding 4 — five of six checkouts ran with every hook silently missing, a DENY
# among them. The hooks are now tracked so they travel with the branch; only per-machine settings and
# autopilot state stay out. Guarded by tools/entry/tracked-hooks.test.mjs.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/autopilot.json
# The compy-entry session store (session records, the Work Control board cache). Before #440 a POSIX
# session resolved it as the RELATIVE folder CompyEntry under its cwd, i.e. inside the checkout. The
# resolver is absolute now; this keeps a copy an older session left behind from ever being committed.
# Guarded by tools/entry/posix-entry-state-dir.test.mjs.
CompyEntry/

# /.agents/ — machine-local, auto-generated `.claude`->Codex mirror of the canonical tracked
# `.claude/skills/`. It is NOT the source of truth (that is `.claude/skills/`, committed); each
# checkout's copy is generated separately and may be stale. Ignored so it is never committed (that
# would double-track the canonical skills) and never dirties the build stamp.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED (`/.agents/`, corrective follow-up 2026-07-20): a bare `.agents/` matches a dir of
# that name at ANY depth, so it could silently hide a real nested project dir that happens to be
# named `.agents`. The leading slash pins the ignore to the repo-root mirror ONLY.
#
# gitignore IS NOT A SKILL-DISABLE MECHANISM: ignoring this dir only keeps it OUT OF GIT — the files
# stay on disk and Codex still DISCOVERS and can load these skills at runtime (Codex reads
# `.codex/`/`.agents/` from the filesystem, not from git's index). So this entry does NOT neutralize
# the mirror for a Codex session; it only stops git from tracking it. To actually stop Codex
# from using it, the dir must be QUARANTINED or DELETED on disk — that is an OWNER decision (it is
# generated, non-obvious, and irreversible without a regenerate step), and it must NOT be regenerated
# until a Codex-native copy is intentionally designed. The reviewable, hand-authored Codex scaffold
# that IS committed and IS the intended source is `AGENTS.md` + `.codex/`.
/.agents/

# Beta distribution kit — locally-assembled artifacts (installer copy, README, invite) for handing
# to testers. Built on demand from committed sources; never committed.
beta-kit/
business/

# Signing keys and secrets — LOCKED rule 4 says the private key NEVER enters the repo / `.env*` / CI.
# This block is the mechanical half of that rule; `scripts/secret-containment-guard.test.mjs` fails the
# build if any of it is deleted or if key material ever becomes tracked.
#
# WIDENED 2026-08-06: `*.key` alone was covering the two keys that exist TODAY (compy-license.key,
# compy-updater.key) while leaving the formats the project is about to need wide open — `.pfx`/`.p12`
# is what an Authenticode code-signing certificate arrives as (an open owner decision), and `.env`
# was named in the rule itself yet had no entry of any kind. A rule that only ignores yesterday's
# filename extensions is not defense-in-depth.
secrets/
*.key
compy-license.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
.env
.env.*
# Sample env files carry no values and SHOULD be reviewable in git.
!.env.example
!.env.sample

# Weekly usage-audit reports (machine-local, auto-written by the CompyUsageAudit scheduled task)
docs/usage-audit/

# machine-local QA evidence (cited from docs but not shipped in the repo)
docs/ui-sweep/shots/

# local build-output staging dir (rel091 worktree stages here; not produced by any tracked script)
release-out/

# Obsidian. `_obsidian/` is Kuya's personal navigation hub for this vault; `.obsidian/` is the app's
# own per-vault config (themes, workspace layout, plugin state) that Obsidian writes into whatever
# folder it opens — here, the repo root. Both are owner tooling, not product code or product docs.
# Root-anchored so neither can shadow a same-named dir elsewhere. On disk only; never enters git,
# never read by agents as product truth.
/_obsidian/
/.obsidian/
